pe":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bootstrap failures (an invalid game definition) are reported to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard error and exit the process with a nonzero status, the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"main.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"--mcp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"code":"GNUSTO_MCP","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") takes the other branch entirely: the process","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"becomes a play-test server speaking MCP on stdio and never builds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world here, because the server builds one ","type":"text"},{"code":"PreparedGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and spins a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world per session. Since every game is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@main struct G: Game, GameMain","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"putting the switch here makes every game that has ever been written","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with this engine — including one whose author has never heard of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"play-test harness — reachable by an agent for the cost of one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".mcp.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entry. See ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlaytestMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"PlaytestServer.serve","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That branch exists only when the package’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Playtest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trait is enabled,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which it is by default. With